# Cohort composition

**What this is.** Every sample's FLARE top-1 ancestry (argmax of its
FLARE proportion vector on chr1, after the
`cohort/merged_groups_rf.tsv` mapping). The bar shows the cohort-wide
count per stratum. Cluster is *not* used as a stratifier — clusters
group samples for upstream processing, not for ancestry reporting.

**How to read this.** Read the bar segments as cohort decomposition.
The supporting table reports each stratum's median across-chrom
stability — the per-sample stdev of the dominant-ancestry proportion
on chr2..22 (lower = more stable cross-chrom calls within the
stratum).

